  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice obligated $7.1B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency recorded 42,188 awards with an average award size of $169K, and obligations were down 16.3% year over year. Annual obligations have moved from $9.1B in FY21 to $7.1B in FY26, with interim totals of $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.4B in FY24, and $8.5B in FY25. Top procurement categories in FY2026 to date include Other Computer Related Services at $828M, Security Guards and Patrol Services at $757M, and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $676M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. leads vendors at $515M, followed by NAPHCARE LLC at $202M and MCKESSON CORPORATION at $166M. This snapshot reflects the Department of Justice’s current fiscal-year-to-date obligations and the major service lines and suppliers driving those obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have Justice's contract obligations changed recently?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $7.1B in FY2026 to date, down 16.3% year over year. Annual obligations were $9.1B in FY21, $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.4B in FY24, and $8.5B in FY25. The FY2026 total is the lowest of the listed fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Justice's biggest contract categories and vendors right now?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest category at $828M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $757M and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $676M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor at $515M, followed by NAPHCARE LLC at $202M and MCKESSON CORPORATION at $166M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Justice spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Justice spends $7.1B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency processed 42,188 awards with an average award size of $169K, and obligations were down 16.3% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Justice buy?",
      "a": "Justice buys services such as Other Computer Related Services ($828M), Security Guards and Patrol Services ($757M), General Medical and Surgical Hospitals ($676M), Other Residential Care Facilities ($482M), and Computer Systems Design Services ($392M). The top ten NAICS categories also include All Other Legal Services ($334M), Custom Computer Programming Services ($270M), Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services ($249M), Facilities Support Services ($219M), and Wired Telecommunications Carriers ($211M)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Justice's largest contractors?",
      "a": "Justice's largest contractors are METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. ($515M), NAPHCARE LLC ($202M), MCKESSON CORPORATION ($166M), AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC ($154M), THE GEO GROUP, INC. ($145M), CGI FEDERAL INC. ($138M), FORFEITURE SUPPORT ASSOCIATES LLC ($131M), HERITAGE HEALTH SOLUTIONS, INC. ($114M), WELLPATH LLC ($110M), and SEVEN CORNERS INC ($110M)."
